From e821aa140b78a41c8b5256b4347fdecd6d967720 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: reaper <theunbounddeveloper@outlook.com>
Date: Tue, 1 Sep 2026 11:35:13 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] v3.0.1: policy routing fail-open, the dead self-heal runner,
 the Warden drops viewer

Four field reports from 2026-09-01 traced to source. The headline finding was in
none of them.

1. FAIL-OPEN (the reason this rung exists). add_multi_routes() - the closed ASUS
   blob - opens with an unconditional IPv4 `ip rule flush`, and wan_up() calls it
   19 lines after start_firewall() installed our policy-routing rules. That wipes
   the whole 9000-9115 pref band while leaving the REAPER_PBR mangle chain
   intact, so the marks keep being set with no rule left to select on. There is
   no iptables backstop: rc/reaper_pbr.c:514-534 is the only enforcement site.
   Result, on every boot and every WAN re-dial: IPv4 traffic pinned to a tunnel
   follows `lookup main` out of the WAN in the clear, and a BLOCK rule (realised
   solely as `prohibit`) stops blocking. Upstream re-asserts its own killswitch
   on the very next line for exactly this reason; we re-asserted nothing.
   reaper_pbr_reassert() now follows all FOUR call sites - wan_up(), the LB
   wan_down() path, wanduck's static-WAN link-up, and the add_multi_routes
   applet in rc.c (whose arms return immediately, so it goes before the return).

2. THE SELF-HEAL RUNNER WAS DEAD CODE, v2.7.3..v3.0.0. rwatch emitted
   `rc reaper_lockrun <script>`, but rc dispatches applets by argv[0] basename
   ONLY: the argv shift for that form is #if 0 in rc.c and DEBUG_RCTEST maps a
   bare "rc" to rctest_main, so every call fell through and did nothing while
   logging that it had re-applied. reaper_lockrun_main was registered but
   reachable only through a /sbin symlink rc/Makefile never created. Install the
   symlink, call the applet by name. This also revives the Warden CRITICAL
   self-heal, dead since the same commit.

3. The ip-rule heal shared heal.n/heal.at with the mark heal, and the mark block
   cleared the counter on every tick whenever the mangle chain was healthy -
   the exact field state - so the five-strike give-up cap was unreachable and the
   heal re-ran every 5 minutes forever. It now owns heal.rn/heal.rat/heal.rgaveup.

4. Warden outbound blocks were never missing from the firewall: they were
   discarded by the GUI. fw_line_is_fwlog() tested for "REAPER-WARDEN " WITH a
   trailing space, which cannot match "REAPER-WARDEN-OUT " or
   "REAPER-WARDEN-SELF " (the next character is '-'), and it is the sole filter
   on action=drops. Dates to v2.3.3, when that prefix was the only one; v2.4.2
   gave outbound its own prefix and did not update the filter.

5. Both /proc/blog/skip_wireguard_network writes now carry a trailing space. The
   kernel handler copy_from_user()s into a 128-byte stack buffer, never
   NUL-terminates it, then runs strsep(" ")/strlen over it and breaks once it
   has the ip token. The trailing space puts strsep's NUL inside the bytes we
   wrote. The del site also moves off `echo`, which appended a newline instead.
   Userspace-only; no kernel change. Not claimed as the cause of the reported
   reboot, which is still unexplained.

Regression pins (build-scripts, synced to the engine): 7 new verify_markers plus
two new reaper_static_checks - pbr-reassert (a C call site leaves no string in
the binary, so a marker structurally cannot express it) and warden-log-prefix
(a producer/consumer contract across rwarden.c, web.c and reaper_diag - the
class of break that stays green through a full build). Both were proven to go
red against the pre-fix tree before being accepted. reaper_diag gains three
runtime FINDINGS for the same faults and goes to v1.3.11.

Deliberately NOT included: the conntrack recapture of flows that leaked while
the rules were absent. With the re-assert now on every wan_up() a purge in the
apply tail would drop every PBR-marked connection on every WAN re-dial; it
belongs on the healer path, where a leak provably happened.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
(cherry picked from commit 546a95f176ade6977c1a48c5c929282e48a29b71)
